# #1099 Stage 2: the Plain Text / Markdown body in QuickMail's own compose window.
# The same steps run against the new editor (UseNewEditor = on) and the current WPF editor (off),
# so the two can be compared. A new message is open, with focus in the To box.
w 4
# Give NVDA a focus change in this window before the test (a relaunch can leave it on the old one).
q +{TAB}
w 2
q {TAB}
w 3

# 0. Reaching the body, by its key and by name.
k %y
w 3
e Message body
n t
w 3
e New Message

# 1. Typed-word echo (#300, #906): each word as Space ends it, and the last as Enter ends it.
#    "the", "cup" and "toast" have letters that are access keys in this window.
t one two the cup toast three
w 3
e one
e two
e the
e cup
e toast
k {ENTER}
w 3
e three

# The rest of the text, typed without logging.
Q Alpha line
q {ENTER}
q {ENTER}
Q Beta line
q {ENTER}
q {ENTER}
q {ENTER}
Q Gamma
q {ENTER}
Q A much longer line of text here
q {ENTER}
Q Short
q {ENTER}
Q End
w 3

# 2. Down from the top: each line once, blank lines as blank (#891).
k ^{HOME}
w 3
e one two the cup toast three
k {DOWN}
w 3
e Alpha line
k {DOWN}
w 3
e blank
e! Beta
k {DOWN}
w 3
e Beta line
k {DOWN}
w 3
e blank
e! Gamma
k {DOWN}
w 3
e blank
e! Gamma
k {DOWN}
w 3
e Gamma

# 3. From the end of a long line, Down onto a shorter one: that line alone.
k {DOWN}
w 3
e A much longer line of text here
k {END}
w 2
k {DOWN}
w 3
e Short
e! End

# 4. Ctrl+Down / Ctrl+Up by paragraph (#1077).
k ^{HOME}
w 3
k ^{DOWN}
w 3
e Alpha line
e! Gamma
k ^{DOWN}
w 3
e blank
k ^{DOWN}
w 3
e Beta line
e! Gamma
k ^{UP}
w 3
e blank
k ^{UP}
w 3
e Alpha line
e! Beta

# 5. Characters and words.
k {HOME}
w 2
k {RIGHT}
w 3
e l
k ^{RIGHT}
w 3
e line

# 6. Leaving and coming back.
k +{TAB}
w 3
e Add
k {TAB}
w 3
e Message body
k %u
w 3
e Subject
k %y
w 3
e Message body

# 7. Spelling: a misspelled word is announced when the caret moves into it, and Alt+1 fixes it.
k ^{END}
w 2
q {ENTER}
Q I recieve mail
w 3
k {HOME}
w 3
k ^{RIGHT}
w 4
e Misspelling: recieve
k %1
w 4
e Replaced with receive
k ^{F7}
w 4
e No misspellings found

# 8. Markdown mode: the switch is announced, and focus stays in the body.
k ^+2
w 4
e Switched to Markdown mode
n {TAB}
w 3
e Message body
